of newsworthy information.

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:27.059
You could get the same value
from watching open testimony

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:28.594
at a New York City
council hearing

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.663
on public access television.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.332
"Yeah, good evening,
council members.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:34.099
My name's Mickey.
I'm from Kew Gardens.

00:05:34.099 --> 00:05:36.469
And my proposal is we replace
the Statue of Liberty

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:39.738
with a statue of Roscoe
the Bed Bug Dog."

00:05:39.738 --> 00:05:41.474
Also, can I just say,

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:43.976
hearing there's a presidential
press conference

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:46.045
is about as exciting
as in Monopoly

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:48.113
when you win second place
in the beauty contest.

00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:50.015
It's like, "Okay,
I guess it's money.

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:51.650
But how'd the old man win?

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.086
Who else was in that
beauty contest, a foot?"

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.355
And because Fox couldn't find
anything else to jump on,

00:05:56.355 --> 00:05:58.157
they decided to spend weeks

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:00.693
obsessing over the whole
press conference thing.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:04.029
-President Biden has now
been in office 43 days

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:07.199
and has not held a single
solo press conference?

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:10.736
-No-show Joe Biden has
been in office 43 days,

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:13.071
still has not held
a single press conference

00:06:13.071 --> 00:06:14.606
since becoming President.

00:06:14.606 --> 00:06:17.376
-Biden has yet to hold
a solo press conference

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:20.279
since he took office
now 46 days ago.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:24.449
-He has not had
a press conference in 48 days.

00:06:24.449 --> 00:06:26.452
-48 days and counting.

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:28.554
-We are halfway
into the first 100 days,

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:33.426
and President Biden still has
not held a solo news conference.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:36.295
-Why hasn't he had
a solo press conference?

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.763
That's the big question.

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:40.532
Is it like the campaign where
he was hiding in the basement?

00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:42.267
-That was his strategy
all the way along,

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:44.303
hide in the basement, don't talk
to the American people.

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:47.673
Now get to the White House, hide
in another figurative basement,

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:49.175
his Oval Office.

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:51.276
-Wait, so is the Oval Office,

00:06:51.276 --> 00:06:53.045
the most famous room
in the world,

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.780
now a figurative basement?

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.548
Once these people come up
with a line they like,

00:06:56.548 --> 00:06:58.217
they never let go of it
no matter how dumb it is.

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:00.686
They're more desperate
to use the "basement" line

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:03.456
than George Costanza was
to use his "jerk store" line.

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:05.158
Hannity's going to start doing
all his monologues

00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:07.059
with a giant bowl of shrimp.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:09.829
Also, at least Biden
goes to the Oval Office.

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:12.431
Trump spent less time there
than a White House tour group.

00:07:12.431 --> 00:07:13.765
Catching Trump
in the Oval Office

00:07:13.765 --> 00:07:16.802
was like catching a station
agent at a subway stop.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:19.671
"Excuse me, the machines are
down, and I need to buy a card."

00:07:19.671 --> 00:07:22.141
"Sorry, shift's over.
I'll be back next leap year."

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.243
They've made such a big deal
out of this press conference

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:27.146
that yesterday Fox News White
House correspondent Peter Doocey

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:29.782
said he had tons of questions
prepared.

00:07:29.782 --> 00:07:31.650
-Do you have a good question
ready?

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:34.754
-I have a binder
full of questions.

00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:36.455
-Is it a Lisa Frank
trapper-keeper?

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:38.490
"Mr. President, I have
a two-part question.

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:42.995
Will you sign my yearbook, and
will you have a great summer?

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:45.631
Thank you, and keep in touch."

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:48.233
Fox has also been full of absurd
and baseless speculation

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:50.469
about what would happen
at this press conference.

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.372
At one point earlier this month,
Fox host Stuart Varney

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.907
predicted that
all of Biden's answers

00:07:54.907 --> 00:07:56.842
would be pre-written
on a teleprompter.

00:07:56.842 --> 00:07:58.644
-What kind of press conference
will it be?

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.045
Will he have a teleprompter?

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:01.880
Will he know the questions
in advance?

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.949
Will he call on friends
and reporters only?

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:06.419
I do believe there'll be
a teleprompter there

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:09.688
which you can just turn on
when you need the set response.

00:08:09.688 --> 00:08:11.824
That would not surprise me
at all.

00:08:11.824 --> 00:08:15.027
And I wouldn't be surprised,
as you say, a staffer saying,

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:17.930
"You ask this question,
you ask that question."

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.798
I can see that
coming a mile off.

00:08:19.798 --> 00:08:21.466
-Maybe Fox News
just can't believe

00:08:21.466 --> 00:08:23.502
that a President would be able
to give a coherent answer

00:08:23.502 --> 00:08:25.304
